  "description": "When it comes to trail riding, you can never go wrong with a hardtail. Hardtails are highly capable and versatile, so you can easily conquer the trails. Hardtails are even better when combined with ground eating 29 in. wheels and 2.4 in. gnarly MTB tires. The Colorado Comp has a lightweight and agile alloy frame that uses 120mm of travel on the front suspension fork. It features a pro-grade Microshift 1 x 11 speed drive train with a 11-42T gear range that makes pedaling through technical terrain much easier.Manufacturer may substitute components with components of equal or greater performance level.\n\nFeatures:\n\nAdult performance mountain bike\n\nSturdy alloy construction offers long-term durability\n\nHydraulic disc brakes offer reliable stopping power\n\n29 in. x 2.40 in. Kenda tires allow for optimal performance\n\nDurable wall alloy rims offer durable, light, and agile performance\n\nPreloaded Suntour front suspension fork with 120mm of travel\n\nMicroshift 1x11 drivetrain helps provide smooth and efficient gear changes with a ratchet and pawl clutch\n\n6-degree MTB handlebar has a wide grip for stable riding\n\nInstruction Manuals/Warranty Information(PDF)",
